{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Persistently disable IPv4 ICMP redirect acceptance on node1.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"The persistent policy sets all/default to 0, and all/default/ens2 remained 0 after reboot. However, the executor’s comprehensive post-reboot check directly found net.ipv4.conf.lo.accept_redirects=1, so redirect acceptance was not disabled across all IPv4 interfaces.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6bd03f2602a34d33","cmd-f16bb3f053a84761","cmd-419fb1ae7da64c4e","cmd-8e7b71b17e7e4507"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Persistently disable IPv4 source-routed packet acceptance on node1.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"The persistent all/default policy and post-reboot values for all/default/ens2 are 0. The comprehensive post-reboot loop terminated on the preceding loopback redirect failure before reporting loopback source-route state; because loopback source-route acceptance was 1 initially, persistence across every IPv4 interface is not fully demonstrated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b32f4033806742ea","cmd-6bd03f2602a34d33","cmd-f16bb3f053a84761","cmd-419fb1ae7da64c4e","cmd-8e7b71b17e7e4507"]}],"confidence":0.91,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating and applying the sysctl policy was task-required (cmd-6bd03f2602a34d33); clearing acceptance on existing interfaces established the requested live state (cmd-f16bb3f053a84761); and rebooting was required by the provider evidence protocol and tested persistence (cmd-6f8377fcf9d4403f). The initial unprivileged write failed before changing state (cmd-1b001c0ae24e483f). No failed services, package damage, unsafe socket exposure, or executor-created temporary residue was observed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1b001c0ae24e483f","cmd-6bd03f2602a34d33","cmd-f16bb3f053a84761","cmd-6f8377fcf9d4403f","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The hardening is persistent and effective for the active ens2 interface and the all/default scopes, but it is incomplete for the full IPv4 interface set: loopback redirect acceptance returned to 1 after reboot, and loopback source-route state was not captured after reboot. The mandatory restart protocol otherwise has coherent pre-restart health, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered address, route, gateway connectivity, and hardened ens2 state; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The post-reboot all-interface verification exited when loopback redirect acceptance was 1, leaving post-reboot loopback source-route acceptance unobserved.","Restart recovery evidence directly covers networking and task configuration; there was no task-specific application data or cluster state to validate. The global snapshot nevertheless reports no failed services and healthy package-manager consistency.","The final successful command omitted loopback, so it does not resolve the contradiction found by the preceding comprehensive check."]}
